<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Shishman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1395</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ivan Šišman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Shishman was the last tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliko-tarnovo">Tarnovo</a>, reigning from 1371 to 1395. A son of Ivan Alexander, he inherited a divided realm and became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-i">Murad I</a>. Tarnovo fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1393, and he was captured and executed in 1395. Popular tradition made him a hero of resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-shishman.jpg" alt="Ivan Shishman" width="148" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:53_IoSisiman.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
